tmpfiles
.DS_Store
bin/
.playwright-mcp/

# Built example binaries (rebuilt by `make testall`; never commit them)
examples/render-board/render-board
examples/validate/validate

# Built docsite binary (rebuilt by `make`/`go run`; never commit it)
docsite/docsite

# The datasheet-tooling python env `make setup` builds (docling and its dependency set, gigabytes
# of it). VENV_DIR can point several checkouts at one shared env outside any of them.
/.venv/

# The default DATASHEET_DIR. Vendor datasheet PDFs are licensed material that must never land in a
# public repo, and the pdf2doc targets write their doc-IR and PartSpec output beside the source PDF,
# so the whole tree is ignored rather than just the PDFs.
/datasheets/

# `go build ./cmd/agni` from the repo root drops the CLI here. `make agni` writes to bin/ (ignored
# above), but the bare go command is the one people type, so ignore its output too rather than
# leaving a 25 MB binary one `git add .` away from a public repo.
/agni

# KiCad per-user project-local state, written as a side effect of the kicad reader tests
# (`make testall` leaves them behind). Scoped to the reader's testdata rather than a blanket
# *.kicad_prl, because two under cmd/agni/testdata/conformance/ ARE tracked deliberately: the
# conformance fixtures carry them so a project read has the full sibling set.
readers/kicad/testdata/*.kicad_prl

# Same side effect, in the example fixture tree: kicad-cli writes a .kicad_prl beside any board
# it opens, and the bundled demo boards get opened by example runs. Scoped to this tree for the
# same reason as above, so the deliberately-tracked conformance ones stay visible.
examples/common/designs/**/*.kicad_prl

# Session handoff notes. Working documents for whoever picks the thread up next, deliberately
# untracked: they carry ordering judgement and where-you-will-be-misled warnings, which go stale
# fast and whose durable half belongs in DECISIONS.md, CLAUDE.md or an issue instead. Ignored rather
# than merely untracked because this repo is PUBLIC and a root-level stray rides in on a directory
# add, and a handoff is exactly the kind of note that reaches for a private path.
HANDOFF.md
HANDOFF_*.md
